Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: put the streams on the clock after the display
 has changed mode

11_25 holds the start of playback while the display is about to change
mode, but only the caching state: the start sync that puts audio and
video on the clock ran before it, against the sound output the mode
change then closes and opens again. After the hold the engine found the
sound about 100 ms off and caught up with a gap of that length a tenth
of a second in, a cut at the start of every film that switched mode.

The start sync now waits as the caching state does, so it runs once the
display reset is done, against the output the film plays on, as it
already did where the mode changed before the sync was reached.

Shared code: the start sync lives only in CVideoPlayer::HandlePlaySpeed.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -2734,7 +2734,9 @@ void CVideoPlayer::HandlePlaySpeed()
       m_VideoPlayerVideo->SendMessage(
           std::make_shared<CDVDMsgDouble>(CDVDMsg::GENERAL_RESYNC, m_clock.GetClock()), 1);
     }
-    else if (video && audio && !deferNoPts)
+    // a mode change about to drop the sound of the link: the streams are put
+    // on the clock after it, not against the output it closes
+    else if (video && audio && !deferNoPts && !HoldForDisplayChange())
     {
       double clock = 0;
       if (m_CurrentAudio.syncState == IDVDStreamPlayer::SYNC_WAITSYNC)
